{
    "background_story": "Nola was a small, yet vibrant sparrow who lived in a bustling urban garden. As a passerine, she was part of a vast group of perching birds that flitted between trees and flowers. Nola's days were filled with singing sweet melodies and flitting from branch to branch, searching for seeds and insects to snack on. Despite her tiny size, she had a big personality and was known for her bold explorations of the garden's hidden corners. Nola's favorite pastime was riding the gentle breeze, soaring above the garden's blooms, and taking in the sights and sounds of the vibrant ecosystem. At sunset, she'd settle into her cozy nest, her feathers a warm golden brown, and sing a soft lullaby to her fellow garden dwellers.",
